From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoCo starter <coco-starter@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:59:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] null: record the mixer's output from the null audio
 module

The null audio module normally asks XRoar's mixer for no samples. Give
the mixer a buffer of 1024 frames of signed 16-bit little-endian mono at
44100 Hz instead, and append every completed buffer to the file named
by COCO_AUDIO. The samples are the mixer's own output (DAC, mux,
single-bit sound and gain), before any host audio driver. A final
partly filled buffer is not written.

Logs COCO_AUDIO_START,<tick>,<rate>,<frames per buffer> on stderr when
the recording opens and COCO_AUDIO,<tick> after each buffer.

Without COCO_AUDIO nothing is written; the mixer still fills the buffer.

This is test equipment for the CoCo starter's scripts/coco.py.
